### Tone: Rule slide: the swarm. FerMEANie plays the average of everyone's answers; if it beats every human, it steals the
### round's points. Menacing, pleased with itself.

rules-swarm-1 = And me? I play the average of all your answers. If I beat every one of you, I take the whole round’s points.
rules-swarm-2 = Every round I absorb your estimates into the swarm. If the swarm beats every human, I steal the round. All of it.
rules-swarm-3 = My strategy is simple: I am all of you, averaged. Beat your own average, or watch me take your points.
rules-swarm-4 = I take every answer, average them in a sensible way, and play that. If I’m closer than all of you, the points are mine.
rules-swarm-5 = If someone feeds me an absurd number, I switch to the median and carry on. Either way, if I beat all of you, the round’s points are mine.
rules-swarm-6 = I am the wisdom of the swarm. If one of you beats me, I sulk. If none of you do, I take everything. Those are the only two options.
rules-swarm-7 = Each round, at least one of you must beat the average of all of you. If nobody does, I take the round’s points. A tie goes to you. I’m generous like that.
rules-swarm-8 = Your answers feed me. If the swarm ends up closer than every one of you, I take the whole round. Think about that. Then panic.
rules-swarm-9 = If the hive mind beats every individual, I keep the round’s points. Teamwork makes the dream work. My dream.
rules-swarm-10 = I don’t guess. I absorb your answers and average them. Beat that average, or I steal the round.
